\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The full pipeline. (1) Observe and probe: from a partial point cloud the robot reasons about support geometry, candidate contacts, and base roundness, and a low planar push measures sliding resistance. (2) Select, tip, and estimate: the mode heuristic (stable pivot? tip before slide? press point usable?) chooses forward tipping or press-and-pull, the interaction runs inside a mode-specific safety margin, and one shared estimator recovers $m$, the CoM, and $\mu _t$ with uncertainty. (3) Plan and validate a task: a feasibility check asks whether the estimates are accurate enough for the task, a physics-informed shove chooses contact height, intensity, and release, and predicted outcomes are compared against observed ones.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flowchart}{{1}{4}{The full pipeline. (1) Observe and probe: from a partial point cloud the robot reasons about support geometry, candidate contacts, and base roundness, and a low planar push measures sliding resistance. (2) Select, tip, and estimate: the mode heuristic (stable pivot? tip before slide? press point usable?) chooses forward tipping or press-and-pull, the interaction runs inside a mode-specific safety margin, and one shared estimator recovers $m$, the CoM, and $\mu _t$ with uncertainty. (3) Plan and validate a task: a feasibility check asks whether the estimates are accurate enough for the task, a physics-informed shove chooses contact height, intensity, and release, and predicted outcomes are compared against observed ones}{figure.1}{}}
