\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Parameter-gated shove-to-region validation. Uninformed geometry-only push heuristics fail in distinct ways on a high-CoM, non-uniform object: a base push tips it backward (the high CoM lags), a top push topples it forward (base friction pins the bottom), and a centroid push chatters because the true CoM is offset from the geometric centroid. The informed push, inside the estimated no-tip window, slides the object into the target. (inset) The admissible push-height window. \textcolor {orange}{SH: From the old draft and illustrative (the ISRR shove video was simulated); replace with hardware frames.}}}{15}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shove}{{10}{15}{Parameter-gated shove-to-region validation. Uninformed geometry-only push heuristics fail in distinct ways on a high-CoM, non-uniform object: a base push tips it backward (the high CoM lags), a top push topples it forward (base friction pins the bottom), and a centroid push chatters because the true CoM is offset from the geometric centroid. The informed push, inside the estimated no-tip window, slides the object into the target. (inset) The admissible push-height window. \sh {From the old draft and illustrative (the ISRR shove video was simulated); replace with hardware frames.}}{figure.10}{}}
\newlabel{eq:hwindow}{{27}{15}{Validation: Parameter-Gated Dynamic Shoving}{equation.10.27}{}}
